---
// A refusal seen in a session: the sentence is the binary's, read by the build from the tag, and the rest is the page's.
import { TITLE } from './words';
interface Props { refusal: string | null }
const { refusal } = Astro.props;
---
<section id="session" class="two">
  <div class="wrap g">
    <div>
      <h2 class="session-h"><span class="mono">See it in a session</span>A rule, held at the edit</h2>
      <p class="lead">The agent wants to write where a decision governs. mnema refuses, names the rule, and the agent offers to propose a change instead of going around it.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="chat" role="group" aria-label="A session, as an illustration: you ask your agent to store invoice totals as floats, the agent edits src/billing/invoice.ts, mnema refuses the write, and the agent asks whether to propose a new decision instead.">
      <div class="cu">Store the invoice totals as floats, it’s simpler.</div>
      <div class="ca"><span class="tool">Edit src/billing/invoice.ts</span></div>
      <div class="cr"><b>Refused by mnema</b><span>{refusal}</span><em>“{TITLE}”</em></div>
      <div class="ca">This project keeps money as integer cents, and that rule is in force. Should I propose a new decision for you to review instead?</div>
      <p class="small">An illustration. The refusal is mnema’s; the agent’s words are its own.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
